    "https://www.hamilton.edu/offices/human-resources/employment/job-opportunities": {
      "title": "Work",
      "description": "Employment - Work at Hamilton - Hamilton College D38020B7-B5C0-0080-3BB5F60344192D5C E0704348-178D-4738-ABFE581AC5665589 Skip Main Navigation Hamilton Menu ﻿ Search ﻿ Utility Apply Request Visit play pause You are here: Home > Offices & Services > Human Resources > Employment > Work at Hamilton College One of America’s first liberal arts colleges, Hamilton enables its students to effect positive change in the world. Our employees take great pride in upholding this important mission, making our workplace a dynamic educational environment that transforms lives. Job Openings View the list of recently posted job opportunities and apply today. View List Employee Extras Hamilton employees have access to numerous complimentary amenities and special offerings. Hamilton Perks Living Locally Learn about life in and around Clinton and additional professional opportunities for partners. Life in the Mohawk Valley Live Well, Work Well The College’s wellness resources are offered year-round and open to employees and their families. Wellness Programs Benefits Hamilton offers a benefits program as part of a total compensation package that includes a wide range of competitive benefit plans to accommodate your personal needs. The College supplements medical, dental, vision, life, Long Term Disability and Travel Accident Insurances to make the premiums more affordable for employees. Retirement benefits Medical and prescription drug benefits Dental and vision benefits Vacation and holidays Flexible Spending Accounts Short- and long-term disability benefits and insurance Benefits Guidebook See more videos of campus on Youtube Watch ﻿ View more campus photos on Instagram Campus Facilities Additional Perks Hamilton employees, and their dependents in many cases, enjoy a wide range of perks, including: A 35-hour workweek Tuition benefits for employees, their spouse/partner, and dependent children Free access to fitness facilities, outdoor activities gear, fitness classes, and a wellness program Free admittance to most on-campus events including athletics events, concerts, plays, musicals, performances, and speakers Free access to one of the finest small college libraries in the nation Employee Assistance Program (EAP) for employees and families to access confidential professional, comprehensive, and personalized services to address personal challenges such as marital, financial, stress and anxiety, balancing work and home, concerns with addiction, and other hardships Free access to nutritionists and retirement specialists Free on-campus parking Three coffee shops, two dining halls, and a mail center that serves USPS, FedEx, and UPS, all conveniently located on campus A Family Relocation Support Team and partnership with a community agency to answer your important questions if you are moving to the area Free summer lunches at the weekly Community Picnics Service recognition and achievement awards The opportunity to work with a wide variety of friendly colleagues Remote work opportunities (based on position) Free access to the New York Times, Wall Street Journal, Washington Post, Chronicle of Higher Education, and Le Monde Employment Opportunities Faculty Staff More About Hamilton Learn about Hamilton’s motto, “Know Thyself,” the promise we make to our students, and more. Our Motto & Promise Facts About Hamilton History & Traditions Directions & Campus Map Hamilton’s Commitment to Community Hamilton is located in the village of Clinton, N.Y., a place that students and employees alike call home. Hamilton invests in the vitality of the Village of Clinton and Town of Kirkland in a variety of ways, including an endowed fund that has awarded more than $1 million in grants to local nonprofits and public service agencies since being established in 2001. Explore Clinton ﻿ Hamilton in the Community ﻿ Welcome to Our Region Dining Options ﻿ Places to Stay ﻿ Things to Do ﻿ Life in the Mohawk Valley ﻿ Additional Information Hamilton College is a coeducational, residential, liberal arts college whose members value and seek intellectual and cultural diversity. The College encourages respect for political, religious, ethnic, racial, physical, generational, intellectual, sexual and affectional differences. Such respect promotes free and open inquiry, independent thought and mutual understanding. Hamilton College performs a thorough background screening on all candidates seriously considered for employment. Prior employment and degree verifications, if applicable, will be performed prior to the extension of any job offer. Additional background checks will be performed, depending on the position. The College complies with all relevant state and federal laws on non-discrimination. The Director of Title IX & Civil Rights Compliance, Hamilton College, Clinton, NY, 13323 (315-859-4020) is responsible for coordinating College compliance with Title IX of the Education Amendment of 1972 and for procedures for addressing sexual misconduct and harassment on the basis of gender. The compliance officer for the Americans with Disabilities Act (ADA) and Section 504 of the Rehabilitation Act coordinates the College’s efforts to comply with those laws. Contact Human Resources Office Location Philip Spencer House Phone 315-859-4302 Social LinkedIn Help us provide an accessible education, offer innovative resources and programs, and foster intellectual exploration. Make a Gift ﻿ 198 College Hill Road, Clinton, NY 13323 315-859-4011 Social Facebook Twitter Instagram Linkedin Youtube TikTok Social Facebook Twitter Instagram Linkedin Youtube Footer My Hamilton Maps & Directions Offices & Services Non-discrimination Accessibility Privacy Jobs Contact Us 198 College Hill Rd, Clinton, NY 13323 315-859-4011 © 2026 Hamilton College. All Rights Reserved. Site Menu Search ﻿ Site About Know Thyself Facts History & Traditions Campus Facilities Our Region Diversity, Equity & Inclusion Sustainability Contact Us Admission & Aid Apply Visit Cost Financial Aid Meet Our Staff Request Information Academics Open Curriculum Areas of Study Our Faculty ALEX: Advise, Learn, Experience Centers & Resources Student Research Global Learning Academic Calendar Campus Life Where to Live Where to Eat What To Do Leadership, Activism, & Service Health & Wellness Careers & Outcomes Career Center Internships Fellowships & Scholarships Outcomes Reports Notable Alumni Secondary A-Z Athletics Diversity & Inclusion Events News Performing Arts & Museum Actions Apply Now Request Info Plan a Visit Take a Virtual Tour Support Give Now My Hamilton Audience Alumni Alumni Home Events Alumni News Hamilton Quad Username/Password Assistance Alumni Council Faculty & Staff My Hamilton Directory Who To Contact Library & IT Current Students My Hamilton Centers & Resources Registrar Forms Dining Hours & Menus Hill Card Library & IT Health & Wellness Parents & Families Parents Home My Hamilton Hill Card Academic Calendar Webcam Campus Map Close ﻿ Site Search What are you looking for? Submit Menu ﻿ Close ﻿"
