    "https://www.hamilton.edu/after": {
      "title": "Careers & Outcomes",
      "description": "Careers & Outcomes - Hamilton College 7ED71F5E-E3C5-9C00-01B08323FFF3E40A B86DABFA-A342-D8BB-E76B1A7ED923A71B Skip Main Navigation Hamilton Menu ﻿ Search ﻿ Utility Apply Request Visit You are here: Home > Careers & Outcomes > Careers & Outcomes Hamilton’s rigorous liberal arts education will teach you how to think, analyze, question assumptions, solve problems, and communicate ideas persuasively – skills that will get you noticed by employers and grad schools. Outcomes Recent graduates are launching careers or taking the next step toward professional degrees. See Where They’re Headed Experiential Learning Hamilton offers numerous options for internships that provide important ways to explore careers. Internships Leaders in Their Field Our alumni live lives of meaning and purpose. Notable Alumni Career Center Connecting students to resources, opportunities, and alumni who share career goals and interests. Career Resources In This Section ﻿ Close ﻿ Navigation Career Center Internships Summer Internship Funding Fellowships & Scholarships Outcomes Reports Class of 2023 Outcomes Report Class of 2022 Outcomes Report Class of 2021 Outcomes Report Notable Alumni After four years on College Hill, you will be well prepared to pursue a graduate degree or enter the work force. 95% of graduates are employed, in graduate school, completing an internship, or pursuing a fellowship within their first year after graduation 94% of graduates had at least one career-related experience, such as an internship or research position 77% of graduates completed at least two career-related experiences Careers and Graduate Schools Hamilton is the perfect size for our students to get personalized attention from faculty advisors and Career Center professionals as they consider careers and grad school options. Meet Recent Graduates Outcomes By The Numbers Internships Nine in 10 of our seniors report having at least one career-­related experience prior to graduating; more than seven in 10 have two. Internship Examples Fellowships and Scholarships Each year our students compete favorably for some of the country’s most prestigious and competitive national fellowships and scholarships. Learn About Recent Recipients The Hamilton Network Whether they serve as a corporate CEO, a world-renowned artist, or a civil rights pioneer, Hamilton alumni return to campus regularly, maintaining ties with former teachers and meeting with students in the classroom, the Career Center, or over a cup of coffee. And in the months following graduation, alumni are there again, welcoming recent graduates to a new city and helping them make personal and professional contacts that launch successful careers. Hill Stops: View a Sampling of Campus Guests Hamilton on LinkedIn Notable Alumni Outcomes Stories Wrisley ’26 Finds a Fit in Product Management at Home Depot ﻿ For Mia Wrisley ’26 finding the right career path meant finding a way to bring together her many interests. After graduation, with a computer science and world politics double concentration, she joined the Home Depot’s inaugural associate product management program in a role she says brings together both the technical and interpersonal skills she developed at Hamilton. Spadaccini’s ’26 Injury Recovery Inspires a Future in Strength & Conditioning ﻿ Edo Spadaccini ’26, an economics and Hispanic studies major from Lexington, Mass., and a Hamilton baseball pitcher, is taking his passion for sports and his own journey back from two injuries as motivation to pursue an master’s degree in strength and conditioning at Springfield College this fall. This summer, he’s interning with the Arizona Diamondbacks. Senior Research, Real-World Impact ﻿ All students at Hamilton complete a senior project, a capstone experience in which they integrate, extend, critique, and apply knowledge gained during their four years on College Hill. The topics vary as much as the students who pursue them — and so do the lessons learned. See the list of senior projects for 2026. “ The formula for businesses trying to compete in today’s economy is simple: hire employees with the mental agility, leadership, and passion to navigate constant change — in other words, hire those who are liberally educated. A. G. Lafley ’69 Retired chairman, president, and CEO of Proctor & Gamble Help us provide an accessible education, offer innovative resources and programs, and foster intellectual exploration. Make a Gift ﻿ 198 College Hill Road, Clinton, NY 13323 315-859-4011 Social Facebook Twitter Instagram Linkedin Youtube TikTok Social Facebook Twitter Instagram Linkedin Youtube Footer My Hamilton Maps & Directions Offices & Services Non-discrimination Accessibility Privacy Jobs Contact Us 198 College Hill Rd, Clinton, NY 13323 315-859-4011 © 2026 Hamilton College. All Rights Reserved. Site Menu Search ﻿ Site About Know Thyself Facts History & Traditions Campus Facilities Our Region Diversity, Equity & Inclusion Sustainability Contact Us Admission & Aid Apply Visit Cost Financial Aid Meet Our Staff Request Information Academics Open Curriculum Areas of Study Our Faculty ALEX: Advise, Learn, Experience Centers & Resources Student Research Global Learning Academic Calendar Campus Life Where to Live Where to Eat What To Do Leadership, Activism, & Service Health & Wellness Careers & Outcomes Career Center Internships Fellowships & Scholarships Outcomes Reports Notable Alumni Secondary A-Z Athletics Diversity & Inclusion Events News Performing Arts & Museum Actions Apply Now Request Info Plan a Visit Take a Virtual Tour Support Give Now My Hamilton Audience Alumni Alumni Home Events Alumni News Hamilton Quad Username/Password Assistance Alumni Council Faculty & Staff My Hamilton Directory Who To Contact Library & IT Current Students My Hamilton Centers & Resources Registrar Forms Dining Hours & Menus Hill Card Library & IT Health & Wellness Parents & Families Parents Home My Hamilton Hill Card Academic Calendar Webcam Campus Map Close ﻿ Site Search What are you looking for? Submit Menu ﻿ Close ﻿"
