    "https://www.hamilton.edu/after/careercenter": {
      "title": "Horowitch Career Center",
      "description": "Horowitch Career Center - Hamilton College 2AAF89FE-DD96-F82A-3AA5A0ED2FDE9576 2BE013DE-1C4A-4A10-AA92407EDA691330 Skip Main Navigation Hamilton Menu ﻿ Search ﻿ Utility Apply Request Visit You are here: Home > Careers & Outcomes > Horowitch Career Center > Horowitch Career Center The liberal arts in practice: empowering students to thrive in any field through career exploration, networking, and skill building. Connect with Your Career Coach Learn how to communicate your value to prospective employers. Meet Career Coaches and Team Career Center Events Check out the upcoming workshops and events offered by the Career Center. View Calendar Handshake Join a Career Community and get access to internships, resources, tools and more. Access Handshake Outcomes Recent graduates are launching careers or taking the next step toward professional degrees. See Where They’re Headed In This Section ﻿ Close ﻿ Navigation About Us Professional Staff Student Staff Resume/Cover Letter Career Communities Arts & Culture Business & Entrepreneurship Communications & Media Education & Social Impact Finance & Consulting Government & Law Health Science, Technology & Analytics Internship/Job Search Job & Internship Listings Interviewing Internship Funding Sadove First Year Internship Program Networking Outcomes For Employers, Alumni & Parents For Parents For Alumni The Maurice Horowitch Career Center is committed to creating a transformative experience for every student, empowering them with best-in-class career resources, individualized support, and a dynamic professional network. Our vision is to provide equitable access for every Hamilton student to services and tools that equip them with the skills, connections, and confidence to excel in their chosen fields. Find your Career Community Our Career Community model connects you to resources, opportunities, and a community of peers and alumni around shared career interests and goals . This integrated, systematic, and accessible industry education approach will guide you through exploration, networking, and skill building within your chosen Career Community. Contact Office / Department Name Maurice Horowitch Career Center Contact Name Front Desk Coordinator Office Location Bristol Center, 3rd Floor Phone 315-859-4346 Email ccadmin@hamilton.edu Hours M – 8:30 a.m.-4:30 p.m. Tu – 8:30 a.m.-4:30 p.m. W – 8:30 a.m.-4:30 p.m. Th – 8:30 a.m.-4:30 p.m. Fr – 8:30 a.m.-4:30 p.m. Social Instagram Career & Internship Stories Students Make Career Connections With Alumni, Parents at NYC Event ﻿ A ‘Know Thyself’ Journey to Columbia Law School ﻿ A Writer's Paradise in Chautauqua ﻿ Dillman ’26 Explores Insurance for Insurers in Summer Internship ﻿ Help us provide an accessible education, offer innovative resources and programs, and foster intellectual exploration. Make a Gift ﻿ 198 College Hill Road, Clinton, NY 13323 315-859-4011 Social Facebook Twitter Instagram Linkedin Youtube TikTok Social Facebook Twitter Instagram Linkedin Youtube Footer My Hamilton Maps & Directions Offices & Services Non-discrimination Accessibility Privacy Jobs Contact Us 198 College Hill Rd, Clinton, NY 13323 315-859-4011 © 2026 Hamilton College. All Rights Reserved. Site Menu Search ﻿ Site About Know Thyself Facts History & Traditions Campus Facilities Our Region Diversity, Equity & Inclusion Sustainability Contact Us Admission & Aid Apply Visit Cost Financial Aid Meet Our Staff Request Information Academics Open Curriculum Areas of Study Our Faculty ALEX: Advise, Learn, Experience Centers & Resources Student Research Global Learning Academic Calendar Campus Life Where to Live Where to Eat What To Do Leadership, Activism, & Service Health & Wellness Careers & Outcomes Career Center Internships Fellowships & Scholarships Outcomes Reports Notable Alumni Secondary A-Z Athletics Diversity & Inclusion Events News Performing Arts & Museum Actions Apply Now Request Info Plan a Visit Take a Virtual Tour Support Give Now My Hamilton Audience Alumni Alumni Home Events Alumni News Hamilton Quad Username/Password Assistance Alumni Council Faculty & Staff My Hamilton Directory Who To Contact Library & IT Current Students My Hamilton Centers & Resources Registrar Forms Dining Hours & Menus Hill Card Library & IT Health & Wellness Parents & Families Parents Home My Hamilton Hill Card Academic Calendar Webcam Campus Map Close ﻿ Site Search What are you looking for? Submit Menu ﻿ Close ﻿"
    },
    "https://www.hamilton.edu/academics/our-faculty": {
      "title": "Our Faculty",
      "description": "Our Faculty - Hamilton College This website uses cookies to offer you a better browsing experience. Accept and Continue Read More / Change Settings B6C583B1-C9C1-2CA6-77DB268184D3A77E B7BA75EF-EF4B-B842-7163A7EDC5B19C8A Skip Main Navigation Hamilton Menu ﻿ Search ﻿ Utility Apply Request Visit You are here: Home > Academics > Our Faculty > Our Faculty Hamilton’s faculty members are accomplished scholars and distinguished teachers. In This Section ﻿ Close ﻿ Navigation Open Curriculum Academic Advising Written & Oral Communication Digital Hamilton Experiential Learning Areas of Study Our Faculty Faculty Directory 2026-27 New Faculty Current Openings Faculty News Dean of Faculty Office ALEX: Advise, Learn, Experience Centers & Resources Student Research Summer Research Programs Support for Projects Senior Fellowship Program Recent Senior Thesis Topics Latest News Global Learning Academic Calendar In the classroom, the lab, the studio and beyond, professors engage actively in the intellectual lives of our students. And don’t be surprised to see them at your concert, basketball game, or supporting your fundraiser. Faculty Directory Our faculty members are active and accomplished scholars who demonstrate extraordinary commitment to and skill in teaching undergraduates. Watch ﻿ Faculty Advising Academic advising at Hamilton helps students make responsible, informed decisions about their intellectual development. Academic Advising Faculty Accomplishments Our faculty members are active and accomplished scholars that demonstrate extraordinary commitment to and skill in teaching undergraduates. Each year, members of the faculty produce an average of 350 papers, books, articles, exhibits, and more. Faculty News Faculty Award Recipients Professors and Students Publish and Present Inside & Outside the Classroom Assistant Professor of Physics Viva Horowitz (center) with summer researchers Maya Kannan ’25 (left) and Sara Conti ’27 (right). Associate Professor of Instruction for Physics Adam Lark works with physics students on the new 20-inch Planewave telescope, a gift from Peter Schloerb ’73. Steven Yao, the Edmund A. LeFevre Professor of English, converses with students. Associate Professor of Biology Rhea Datta teaching Explorations in Biology: Coming to Life – Embryogenesis and Development. In the spacious acting studio, students perform under the watchful eye of Associate Professor of Theatre Mark Cryer. Assistant Professor of Digital Arts Anna Huff helps her students prepare for the next episode of TV CLUB. Help us provide an accessible education, offer innovative resources and programs, and foster intellectual exploration. Make a Gift ﻿ 198 College Hill Road, Clinton, NY 13323 315-859-4011 Social Facebook Twitter Instagram Linkedin Youtube TikTok Social Facebook Twitter Instagram Linkedin Youtube Footer My Hamilton Maps & Directions Offices & Services Non-discrimination Accessibility Privacy Jobs Contact Us 198 College Hill Rd, Clinton, NY 13323 315-859-4011 © 2026 Hamilton College. All Rights Reserved. Site Menu Search ﻿ Site About Know Thyself Facts History & Traditions Campus Facilities Our Region Diversity, Equity & Inclusion Sustainability Contact Us Admission & Aid Apply Visit Cost Financial Aid Meet Our Staff Request Information Academics Open Curriculum Areas of Study Our Faculty ALEX: Advise, Learn, Experience Centers & Resources Student Research Global Learning Academic Calendar Campus Life Where to Live Where to Eat What To Do Leadership, Activism, & Service Health & Wellness Careers & Outcomes Career Center Internships Fellowships & Scholarships Outcomes Reports Notable Alumni Secondary A-Z Athletics Diversity & Inclusion Events News Performing Arts & Museum Actions Apply Now Request Info Plan a Visit Take a Virtual Tour Support Give Now My Hamilton Audience Alumni Alumni Home Events Alumni News Hamilton Quad Username/Password Assistance Alumni Council Faculty & Staff My Hamilton Directory Who To Contact Library & IT Current Students My Hamilton Centers & Resources Registrar Forms Dining Hours & Menus Hill Card Library & IT Health & Wellness Parents & Families Parents Home My Hamilton Hill Card Academic Calendar Webcam Campus Map Close ﻿ Site Search What are you looking for? Submit Menu ﻿ Close ﻿"
    },
    "https://www.hamilton.edu/after/fellowships": {
      "title": "Fellowship Advising",
      "description": "Fellowship Advising - Hamilton College This website uses cookies to offer you a better browsing experience. Accept and Continue Read More / Change Settings 05D340BA-DF28-3517-88F6DD8B085E0160 D6912D7A-ADFF-46A8-A9E2E0B61DD90A45 Skip Main Navigation Hamilton Menu ﻿ Search ﻿ Utility Apply Request Visit You are here: Home > Academics > Centers & Resources > Fellowship Advising > Fellowship Advising The Office of Student Fellowship helps Hamilton students and recent alumni connect with transformative experiences and opportunities. Fellowship Advising Students work with the Director to identify and apply for nationally competitive opportunities. Getting Started Join Us! Check out the upcoming information sessions and events offered by the Fellowships Advising. See Calendar International Summer Research Funding Hamilton’s new program supports students who wish to conduct summer research outside the U.S. About the Program Frequently Asked Questions Who should consider applying? When should I start the process? What makes a strong application? See Answers Recent Award Recipients Each year our students compete favorably for some of the country’s most prestigious fellowships. Fellowship & Scholarship Recipients In This Section ﻿ Close ﻿ Navigation Planning Ahead Upcoming Events & Deadlines Award Opportunities Award Recipients Frequently Asked Questions International Summer Research Awards The process of applying for fellowships helps candidates clarify goals, define resources, identify mentors, and develop tools applicable to all aspects of their lives. We encourage all candidates to be intrepid in pursuing fellowship opportunities that will expand both their worldview and their perspective on themselves. See FAQs See Upcoming Events Fellowships Team Melissa Welshans Director of Student Fellowships mwelshan@hamilton.edu 315-859-4775 Melissa Welshans, who joined Hamilton College in July 2026, is excited to support students in their pursuit of national fellowships and scholarships. She holds a Ph.D. in English Literature from Syracuse University and previously served as the assistant director of Syracuse's fellowships office. She believes in the value of the application process regardless of the outcome, and hopes that all applicants come away from the experience with a deeper understanding of themselves and the impact they hope to have on the world. Dylann McLaughlin Office Coordinator dmclaugh@hamilton.edu 315-859-4258 Dylann previously worked as a public school English teacher in Utica and Clinton school districts. She holds her MAT in Secondary Education and BA in English from Colgate University. At Hamilton, she supports the Office of Student Fellowships as well as ALEX Advising and Art History. She coordinates programming and operations for these offices as well as the First-Year Course mentor program. 2026 Fellowship Award Recipients Caroline Boies ’26 ﻿ William M. Bristol Fellowship About Caroline Caroline Boies ’26, a math and art double major, will study the way refugees and immigrants use food to foster community, specifically “how food functions not only as a connection to home, but also as a tool for adaptation and belonging in unfamiliar environments.” She plans to travel to India, Denmark, France, Chile, and Australia to experience a wide variety of “political infrastructures, histories of immigration, and geographic contexts.” Sara Conti ’27 ﻿ Barry Goldwater Scholarship About Sara Sara Conti '27, a mathematics and physics double major, is a 2026 Barry Goldwater Scholar whose passion lies in particle physics. Last summer, she researched neutrino interactions by simulating activity in a South Pole detector, and this summer she is transitioning into a more experimental role. After graduation, Conti plans to pursue a Ph.D. and a career in research. Mele Kaneali’i ’27 ﻿ Harry S. Truman Scholarship About Mele Mele Kaneali’i ’27 is Hamilton’s latest — and fourth ever — recipient of the prestigious Harry S. Truman Scholarship, a graduate fellowship awarded to college juniors pursuing careers in public service. After graduating from Hamilton, the government major intends to pursue a J.D. and a master's of urban and regional planning in housing policy. Arshdeep Kaur ’26 ﻿ Thomas J. Watson Fellowship About Arshdeep Arshdeep Kaur ’26, a biology major, will explore how communities and healthcare systems address disparities in cancer prevention, diagnosis, and treatment for her project, Bridging Gaps in Global Cancer Care Access. Kaur plans to travel to India, South Africa, Australia, and the United Kingdom. Elise Kwon ’26 ﻿ William M. Bristol Fellowship About Elise Elise Kwon ’26, a biochemistry major and music minor, will travel with her violin to explore how music can foster community and help people navigate feelings such as grief and belonging, creating a “living archive of musical healing practices.” Thus far, she plans to travel to South Korea, India, and South Africa, chosen for their “rich musical traditions and strong community-based healing practices.” Xavier McMahon ’27 ﻿ Critical Language Scholarship About Xavier Xavier McMahon ’27, a Russian studies and world politics double major, has won a second Critical Language Scholarship (CLS). Last summer, he studied Russian in Daugavpils, Latvia. This summer he will focus on Mandarin in Tainan, Taiwan. Lucy Meola ’26 ﻿ Thomas J. Watson Fellowship About Lucy Lucy Meola ’26, environmental studies and anthropology double major, will research rewinding, a novel approach to conservation where humans take an active role in restoring degraded ecosystems. She will examine how people can develop more hopeful and resilient forms of environmentalism. Meola plans to travel to five countries—Scotland, Chile, Argentina, Uzbekistan, and Namibia. Emma Wilson ’27 ﻿ Barry Goldwater Scholarship About Emma Emma Wilson '27, a physics major, is a 2026 Barry Goldwater Scholar with interests spanning experimental and theoretical physics. She has conducted research on neutron scattering and improving neutron polarization efficiency, and this summer she will explore quantum gravity alongside Professor Seth Major. After graduation, Wilson is considering a gap year to work in a lab or develop her science communication skills before pursuing a Ph.D. in physics. 2025 Fellowship Award Recipients Sabina Feder ’25 ﻿ William M. Bristol Fellowship About Sabina Feder, a food studies major, took classes in literature, anthropology, and environmental science to create her own interdisciplinary major at Hamilton and prepare for her project “Waste Not: Local Initiatives Against Global Food Waste.” She will visit New Zealand, the Bahamas, the Netherlands, and Sweden. Andrew Fredericks ’25 ﻿ Thomas J. Watson Fellowship About Andrew Fredericks’ Watson will take him to countries with exciting human evolutionary discoveries: Germany, Georgia, and Kenya for their fossil sites of early hominins, and Brazil for its population of chimpanzees that have developed a unique ability to use tools. Charlie Haberstock ’25 ﻿ Thomas J. Watson Fellowship About Charlie Haberstock’s Watson project will take him to some of the most isolated towns in Canada, Finland, Greenland, and Tristan da Cunha, the world’s most remote inhabited island. He plans to study the issues faced by remote economies as globalization leads to a dangerous feedback loop of economic depression and depopulation. Naval Lappalainen ’25 ﻿ Critical Language Scholarship About Naval Naval Lappalainen ’25, a double major in history and Russian studies, from Wilmington, Del., will study in Kyrgyzstan. Xavier McMahon ’27 ﻿ Critical Language Scholarship About Xavier Xavier McMahon ’27, a double major in world politics and Russian studies from Louisville, Kentucky, will be based in Daugavpils, Latvia. Quentin Messer ’26 ﻿ Harry S. Truman Scholarship About Quentin A world politics concentrator, Messer plans to pursue a J.D. and Master’s in Public Administration (MPA) following graduation. He is Hamilton’s third recipient of the prestigious award following Dewayne Martin ’24 and Frederick Nelson ’78. Yuxuan Xu ’26 ﻿ Goldwater Scholarship About Yuxuan Xu is currently spending the semester at the Marine Biological Laboratory in Woods Hole, Mass., where he’s exploring how marine organisms can reveal insights into human biology. His time at Woods Hole has him excited for a future in science; he has ambitions to earn a Ph.D. in neuroscience, the inspiration for which he attributes to Professor of Biology Emeritus Herman Lehman. More Fellowships News Five Seniors Receive Fulbright ETAs ﻿ Five members of Hamilton’s Class of ’26 will be leaving College Hill for classrooms abroad through the prestigious Fulbright English Teaching Assistantship program. Mele Kaneali'i ’27 Awarded Truman Scholarship ﻿ Mele Kaneali'i ’27 is Hamilton’s latest — and fourth ever — recipient of the prestigious Harry S. Truman Scholarship, a graduate fellowship awarded to college juniors pursuing careers in public service. After graduating from Hamilton, the government major intends to pursue a J.D. and a master of urban and regional planning in housing policy. Boies ’26 and Kwon ’26 Awarded Bristol Fellowships for International Travel ﻿ Caroline Boies ’26, a math and art double major, and Elise Kwon ’26, a biochemistry major and music minor, have both been awarded the William M. Bristol Jr. ’17 Fellowship for International Travel, providing them the opportunity to engage in independent studies abroad. The fellowship sponsors projects “based on strong personal interest and commitment” and that “exhibit a spirit of inquisitiveness and a seriousness of purpose.” 50 Years of Watson Fellows ﻿ Though their projects and itineraries couldn’t have been more varied, Hamilton’s Watson Fellows all describe their experience as life-changing. We caught up with a few to mark the program’s 50th anniversary. Contact Office / Department Name Student Fellowships Contact Name Melissa Welshans Director of Student Fellowships Office Location Bristol Center Phone x4775 Email mwelshan@hamilton.edu Webpage Schedule an Appointment through Compass Social Instagram LinkedIn Help us provide an accessible education, offer innovative resources and programs, and foster intellectual exploration. Make a Gift ﻿ 198 College Hill Road, Clinton, NY 13323 315-859-4011 Social Facebook Twitter Instagram Linkedin Youtube TikTok Social Facebook Twitter Instagram Linkedin Youtube Footer My Hamilton Maps & Directions Offices & Services Non-discrimination Accessibility Privacy Jobs Contact Us 198 College Hill Rd, Clinton, NY 13323 315-859-4011 © 2026 Hamilton College. All Rights Reserved. Site Menu Search ﻿ Site About Know Thyself Facts History & Traditions Campus Facilities Our Region Diversity, Equity & Inclusion Sustainability Contact Us Admission & Aid Apply Visit Cost Financial Aid Meet Our Staff Request Information Academics Open Curriculum Areas of Study Our Faculty ALEX: Advise, Learn, Experience Centers & Resources Student Research Global Learning Academic Calendar Campus Life Where to Live Where to Eat What To Do Leadership, Activism, & Service Health & Wellness Careers & Outcomes Career Center Internships Fellowships & Scholarships Outcomes Reports Notable Alumni Secondary A-Z Athletics Diversity & Inclusion Events News Performing Arts & Museum Actions Apply Now Request Info Plan a Visit Take a Virtual Tour Support Give Now My Hamilton Audience Alumni Alumni Home Events Alumni News Hamilton Quad Username/Password Assistance Alumni Council Faculty & Staff My Hamilton Directory Who To Contact Library & IT Current Students My Hamilton Centers & Resources Registrar Forms Dining Hours & Menus Hill Card Library & IT Health & Wellness Parents & Families Parents Home My Hamilton Hill Card Academic Calendar Webcam Campus Map Close ﻿ Site Search What are you looking for? Submit Menu ﻿ Close ﻿"
    }
